"The `trend_switch` timer is in place: Python and the JavaScript port match exactly, there is one new golden case, and the \"Beat the S&P: 2x trend (CA)\" button is on the website. Every pre-existing golden result is unchanged. Nothing was deployed, git wasn't used, and the Pages repo wasn't touched.\n\n## Test results\n- **`tools/gen_golden.py --check`**: 27 cases verified, exit 0. The 29 pre-existing golden JSON files (including `golden/validation/*`) have the same sha256 as before; only `golden/manifest.json` changed.\n- **Validation goldens**: the generator has no `--check` flag, so I re-ran both cases with a scratch script. `validate_price_only` (30 combos) and `validate_all_pickers` (100 combos) are byte-identical.\n- **`.venv/bin/python -m pytest golden reference -q`**: 42 passed (29 golden + 13 reference, of which 5 are new).\n- **`cd web/engine && npm test`**: 52 of 52 pass, 0 fail. That includes 27 parity cases with the new one at 1e-9, 2 validation parity cases and 4 new trend-switch tests.\n- **The site's own JS path** (the code the browser actually runs), run on the new golden case: 25,128 values compared, 0 mismatches. The exact request the preset button sends gives the same after-tax CAGR to the last bit.\n- **`tools/build_web_data.py --verify`**: 537 tickers round-trip. `universe.bin`, `calendar.bin`, `fundamentals.json` and `sp500-pit.json` are byte-identical to before. `tickers/SSO.bin(.gz)` and `tickers/IEF.bin(.gz)` exist. `tools/gen_web_metadata.py` reports 11 timers and 537 tickers.\n- **`cd web/frontend && npm run build`**: succeeds.\n\n## Cross-check: lab vs site (CA rates, 5+5 bps)\n| window | site after-tax | lab (cached `sweep` record, full/CA) | gap (pp) | lab without monthly rebalance | SPY after-tax (both) | switches | daily state and switch dates |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2006-07-01\u21922026-07-01 | 13.424% | 13.342% | +0.081 | 13.424% | 9.672% | 24 | identical |\n| 2007-01-01\u21922026-07-01 (golden) | 12.968% | 12.886% | +0.082 | 12.968% | 9.339% | 24 | identical |\n| 2008-01-01\u21922013-01-01 | 11.316% | 11.449% | \u22120.133 | 11.316% | 1.324% | 5 | identical |\n| 2010-01-01\u21922020-01-01 | 14.844% | 14.659% | +0.184 | 14.844% | 10.750% | 8 | identical |\n| 2015-01-01\u21922025-01-01 | 12.679% | 12.572% | +0.107 | 12.679% | 10.529% | 12 | identical |\n| 2016-07-01\u21922026-07-01 | 13.321% | 13.279% | +0.042 | 13.321% | 12.603% | 14 | identical |\n| 2019-01-01\u21922024-01-01 | 10.581% | 10.353% | +0.228 | 10.581% | 12.023% | 9 | identical |\n| 2021-01-01\u21922026-07-01 | 9.595% | 9.702% | \u22120.107 | 9.595% | 11.813% | 10 | identical |\n\n- **Why the gaps above 0.05 pp exist:** they come entirely from how cash is handled, as you expected.\n  - The lab rebalances back to 100% of the held fund every month. In January that means selling shares to pay the prior year's tax, which realizes more taxable gain.\n  - The site only trades on a switch. The January tax bill is left as negative cash, effectively a 0% loan, until the next switch.\n  - The site comes out ahead in rising windows and behind in falling ones.\n  - Proof: running the same lab rule without the monthly rebalance (`sdrift=None`) matches the site to within 1.3e-5 pp in all 8 windows. The tiny remainder is the lab's 0.999999 cash-scaling factor.\n  - The negative cash is a 0%-interest loan, which slightly flatters the site version in rising markets.\n- **Switch dates 2006\u21922026:** 2006-07-03 SSO, 2007-08-15 IEF, 2007-09-18 SSO, 2007-11-12 IEF, 2009-05-08 SSO, 2010-05-20 IEF, 2010-09-20 SSO, 2011-08-04 IEF, 2012-01-04 SSO, 2015-08-21 IEF, 2016-03-29 SSO, 2018-10-24 IEF, 2019-03-15 SSO, 2020-02-28 IEF, 2020-06-02 SSO, 2022-02-22 IEF, 2022-03-29 SSO, 2022-04-22 IEF, 2023-01-23 SSO, 2023-10-27 IEF, 2023-11-10 SSO, 2025-03-11 IEF, 2025-05-16 SSO, 2026-03-26 IEF, 2026-04-14 SSO.\n- **Lab summary (full protocol):** +3.67 pp over SPY for the full period, and it beats SPY in 100% of 10-, 15- and 20-year windows and 88.5% of 5-year windows.\n- **Data copy:** fresh lab runs on the copied `data/` files reproduce the cached sweep values exactly.\n\n## Caveats\n- **Drawdown:** the golden case's worst after-tax drawdown is \u221248.5%, from 2022-01-03 to 2023-03-13 (\u221242.0% pre-tax). Stocks and Treasuries fell together then. SPY's worst over the same window was \u221255.2%, in 2008\u201309. The timer's \"Learn more\" text and the new trust item both say this.\n- **Universe exclusion was needed:** without it, SSO and IEF would have changed every \"all\"-universe case, including the seeded random picker. I added `UNIVERSE_EXCLUDE = {\"SSO\",\"IEF\"}` and applied it in:\n  - the Python service, `walkforward.py` and `grid_combos.py`\n  - `universe.bin` (the manifest now records the list)\n  - the JS service, with a unit test that checks the JS list matches the manifest\n\n  Both tickers stay available for manual mode, menus and ticker search.\n- **Sweeps skip the new timer:** `trend_switch` is in `TIMERS`, but the grid, walk-forward and validation sweeps use a new `SWEEP_TIMERS` that leaves it out. Otherwise both validation goldens would have changed (the JS sweep already lists exactly 10 timers).\n- **It still shows in picker mode:** the timer appears in the timer grid there, where it would just hold cash; its description says it is meant for manual mode.\n- **Research lab, not fixed:** `research/lab/data.py::site_tickers()` now sees SSO and IEF. That only matters for lab configs using the \"all\" universe; none currently do, and the point-in-time S&P universe is unaffected. I left it alone because `data.py` is part of every lab cache key, so editing it would invalidate the whole 4.4 GB run cache while Round-2 agents are using it. The fix is one line: filter `UNIVERSE_EXCLUDE` in `site_tickers()`. The lab now also reads SSO and IEF from `data/`; the rows are identical.\n- **\"Validate\" on this preset:** the out-of-sample check ignores `warmup_days` (existing behaviour in both Python and JS), so in that run the rule holds cash for its first 175 trading days.\n- **Manifest:** only the new case entry and the data fingerprint changed (538 \u2192 540 files). The `env` block was left as it was because git was unavailable.\n- **Not requested but done:** I added company names for SSO and IEF to `data/company_names.csv` so search finds them by name. I also changed the manual-mode trust item for all-fund baskets: it now warns about choosing funds with hindsight instead of \"today's survivors\".\n- **Docs left stale:** the case counts in `README.md` and `reference/README.md` were already out of date before this change and I didn't update them.\n\n## Files changed\n**Modified:**\n- /Users/siddhartha/dev/StockTest/strategies/timers.py\n- /Users/siddhartha/dev/StockTest/backtester/data.py\n- /Users/siddhartha/dev/StockTest/reference/service.py\n- /Users/siddhartha/dev/StockTest/reference/catalog.py\n- /Users/siddhartha/dev/StockTest/reference/tests/test_reference.py\n- /Users/siddhartha/dev/StockTest/walkforward.py\n- /Users/siddhartha/dev/StockTest/grid_combos.py\n- /Users/siddhartha/dev/StockTest/download_data.py\n- /Users/siddhartha/dev/StockTest/tools/build_web_data.py\n- /Users/siddhartha/dev/StockTest/tools/gen_golden.py\n- /Users/siddhartha/dev/StockTest/golden/manifest.json\n- /Users/siddhartha/dev/StockTest/data/company_names.csv\n- /Users/siddhartha/dev/StockTest/STRATEGY_CATALOG.md\n- /Users/siddhartha/dev/StockTest/web/engine/src/timers.js\n- /Users/siddhartha/dev/StockTest/web/engine/src/universe.js\n- /Users/siddhartha/dev/StockTest/web/engine/src/service.js\n- /Users/siddhartha/dev/StockTest/web/engine/src/walkforward.js (comment only)\n- /Users/siddhartha/dev/StockTest/web/engine/test/parity.test.js\n- /Users/siddhartha/dev/StockTest/web/engine/test/validation.test.js\n- /Users/siddhartha/dev/StockTest/web/engine/test/worker.test.js (counts 535\u2192537, 10\u219211 timers)\n- /Users/siddhartha/dev/StockTest/web/frontend/src/App.jsx\n- /Users/siddhartha/dev/StockTest/web/frontend/src/content.js\n- /Users/siddhartha/dev/StockTest/web/frontend/src/components/Results.jsx\n- /Users/siddhartha/dev/StockTest/web/frontend/src/components/TimerGrid.jsx (comment only)\n\n**New:**\n- /Users/siddhartha/dev/StockTest/data/SSO.csv (5,038 rows, 2006-06-21\u21922026-07-01)\n- /Users/siddhartha/dev/StockTest/data/IEF.csv (6,019 rows, 2002-07-30\u21922026-07-01)\n- /Users/siddhartha/dev/StockTest/golden/manual_trendswitch_sso_ief.json\n- /Users/siddhartha/dev/StockTest/web/engine/test/trendswitch.test.js\n\n**Rebuilt (generated, not hand-edited):** in `build/webdata/`, `manifest`, `catalog`, `tickers` and `search.json` plus the new SSO/IEF ticker files; and `web/frontend/dist`.\n\n**Scratch scripts:** /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-siddhartha-dev-StockTest/30740174-6df3-42fd-9108-dbc7a9c13aa4/scratchpad/ holds `crosscheck.py`, `gen_one.py`, `check_validation.py` and `service_check.mjs`."